# Hero walk cycle. Four 32x32 frames on one 128x32 strip, facing right.
#
# Contact / passing / contact / passing. Both soles are on row 31 at contact;
# at passing the swinging boot lifts 1px and the body rides 1px higher, because
# a walk raises the hips when the support leg straightens. Lifting the whole
# sprite off the floor instead would read as hopping -- the corsair strip in
# assets/experiments made the same call.
#
# Only the right-facing set exists. mirror(hero-f3-walk-left) was already
# byte-identical to hero-f4-walk-right, so the second facing was a redundant
# texture; Player draws this one with SpriteEffects.FlipHorizontally.
#
# The two contact frames share an upper body and differ only in which leg
# carries the light ramp. At a 16px-wide silhouette that shading IS the read:
# there is no room to swing an arm and no room for perspective.
#
# Posed from a generated reference sheet that could not be imported -- it
# measured 1024x559 at 1:1 with 105,888 colours and conformed at 0.0558 mean
# delta, over the 0.05 "regenerate, don't fix" line. The poses survived; none
# of its pixels did. See assets/WORKFLOW.md.
name hero-walk
size 128 32
frames 4
key o outline
key b blue-3
key B blue-4
key h blue-5-hilite
key m blue-2-mid
key s blue-0-shadow
key w warm-2-mid
key W warm-3
key S warm-0-shadow
key a warm-4
key A accent-rust
key r warm-1
key H warm-5-hilite
pixels
